      "message": "`sed -i -e \u0027s@(^|\\s|\")bazel-out/@\\1%s/@g\u0027 \u0027%s\u0027`\n\nshould be safer as it prevents bash from interpreting the paths and easier to read with fewer `\\` chars\n\n`s@@@` (as opposed to `s///`) will also allow us to remove the path separator replacement for bazelOutDir\n\nthe `/` after `bazel-out` will also protect us from replacing non-directories that start with `bazel-out`, e.g. `bazel-output.txt`",
